      q2: 'Why does Niffler report insufficient balance or quota?', a2: 'Check your wallet balance, remaining plan quota, and plan expiry. Also verify any independent quota assigned to the API key.',
      q3: 'Why is a model missing or not permitted?', a3: 'Copy the exact model ID from the marketplace and confirm that the API key is allowed to use it. A model may also be temporarily offline for maintenance.',
      q4: 'Are failed requests billed?', a4: 'Requests that produce no valid usage are not normally settled, but usage records are authoritative. An upstream may consume tokens before returning an error.',
      q5: 'Can Claude Code, Codex CLI, and Gemini CLI share one key?', a5: 'They can, but separate keys are recommended for permissions, cost attribution, and independent revocation.',
      q6: 'How can I see which model or route handled a request?', a6: 'Open usage records in the dashboard and locate the request by time or API key to inspect its model, usage, cost, status, and available route information.',
